306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:40:06','2016-08-19 18:40:06','Adds a ton of fun to the original game.  Great to spice up a board game night.  Definitely adults only ;)',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(172,2576,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:41:02','2016-08-19 18:41:02','Great classic!  Re-designed more modern version too. Highly recommend.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(173,2927,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:42:19','2016-08-19 18:42:19','Woah, this little ditty takes Laser Khet to a whole new level!  Seriously challenging but highly recommend, it makes the game much more interesting.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(174,2607,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:43:24','2016-08-19 18:43:24','Fun, cheeky game, good for groups.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(175,2593,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:46:08','2016-08-19 18:46:08','Super popular game for large groups. You can play with basically unlimited amount of people so no one is left out!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(176,2667,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:48:16','2016-08-19 18:48:16','Hilarious card game. Get unofficial expansion to cards against humanity but you dont really even need the original to play.  GREAT GIFT!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(177,2637,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:49:13','2016-08-19 18:49:13','Super silly and very easy to learn.  Cute game for kids too,  save those kittens!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(178,2605,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:53:07','2016-08-19 18:53:07','Fantastic party game.  This game combines a betting & gambling component which is super fun.  I am going to buy multiple copies for family as gifts.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(179,2654,'lyndsey','lyndsey@boardgames.com','','2600:8801:c306:4a00:25fe:fb11:dfa9:2e4','2016-08-19 11:58:53','2016-08-19 18:58:53','I really love this game.  Easy to learn and has very unique theme, with just the right about of backstabbing.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,5),(186,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:33','2016-08-24 11:37:33','PDT payment completed',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(187,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:33','2016-08-24 11:37:33','Order status changed from Pending Payment to Processing.',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(188,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:34','2016-08-24 11:37:34','Item ZMG71570 stock reduced from 2 to 1.',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(189,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:34','2016-08-24 11:37:34','Item NSG150 stock reduced from 5 to 4.',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(190,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:34','2016-08-24 11:37:34','Item ASK100 stock reduced from 491 to 490.',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(191,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 04:37:34','2016-08-24 11:37:34','IPN payment completed',0,'1','WooCommerce','order_note',0,0),(193,2593,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 07:43:28','2016-08-24 14:43:28','Apples to Apples is an absolute classic that in a way, started an entire movement in gaming.  It is basically the family version of Cards Against Humanity, which stole it\'s gameplay directly from Apples to Apples.\r\n\r\nThis game really tells you a lot of about your friends and family.  Above all, you find out who is a straight-shooter, and who is a goof ball.  It\'s all about knowing the judge.  \r\n\r\nFor example, when my brother is the judge you have no prayer if you play a card that actually makes sense.  The more ridiculous the card, the better your chances of winning.\r\n\r\nWe\'ve played countless games of Apples to Apples and apparently with the high sales volume so have many others.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(194,2666,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 07:45:11','2016-08-24 14:45:11','This is a simple, yet fun party game.  Really a brilliant twist on Pictionary or Win Lose or Draw.  This is a great one for the holidays or family gathering, but would also work well with a group of friends.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(195,2703,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 07:47:50','2016-08-24 14:47:50','First off, I\'ve got to say that I learned something from this game.  I had no idea that peppers had a heat index called their scoville rating.  Being a lover of hot food that is kinda cool.\r\n\r\nIn regard to the game, it is really well designed.  This is one of those perfect games for people who want to try something new, but don\'t like overly complicated instructions.\r\n\r\nIt requires a good amount of foresight as you can easily \"paint yourself in a corner\" if you are not careful.\r\n\r\nWe really enjoyed the gameplay as well as the art and all the little hot pepper components.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(197,2571,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:18:57','2016-08-24 15:18:57','I babysat my baby nephew one summer and we played Candy Land almost every day.  He learned his colors by playing this game.  True classic.\r\n\r\nNote that I\'m not implying that this is a ton of fun for adults, other than the fun you have watching kids have fun.  \r\n\r\nI know I am at risk of hearing it from the board game experts out there for this 5 star rating, but if it wasn\'t a good game it wouldn\'t still be around.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(198,2603,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:29:49','2016-08-24 15:29:49','Love this game!  To me, it isn\'t just the actual gameplay that makes a game fun.  It\'s a lot about the excitement of the players and the smacktalk.  This game has tons of both.\r\n\r\nFirst off, you play the game inside of a wrestling ring, complete with ropes, turnbuckles and all.  It\'s a dice rolling game and if your dice land outside of the ring they don\'t count (which means you can try to knock your opponent\'s dice out).\r\n\r\nThe game itself is pretty darn cool.  Simple enough to learn pretty quickly, with a few \"advanced\" features so that the replayability is good.  They did an awesome job with the characters and back stories, and each character has special moves which is a ton of fun.\r\n\r\nI think the best part of this game is that they included 2 championship belts.  I\'m honestly itching to play this game again because Danny and Andrew hold the belts.  And trust me, that have not let Derek and I forget!\r\n\r\n\r\nTo me, a tabletop game is great when people get excited to play it.  We first played this one when we were in Vegas for a board game convention.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(199,2548,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:30:42','2016-08-24 15:30:42','This is one of those games I wish I could give 6 stars.  It is simple, yet engaging.  It keeps everyone involved the entire time and it has more strategy than you might think.  I love it because it is small in its package and you can play it with any type of crowd.  I have given this game as a gift many times and cannot recommend it highly enough!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(200,2674,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:32:37','2016-08-24 15:32:37','One of the all time classics, I love this game because it does something few games do: create a high amount of strategy with VERY simple rules.  One of those games that you think \"oh, this is easy\" until you realized you messed up and you\'re getting your butt kicked.  \r\n\r\nDespite not being sold in big box retail outlets, this game is still one of the best sellers of all time.  If you haven\'t played it, you need to get it.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(201,2579,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:37:18','2016-08-24 15:37:18','This game was designed by a game design legend, the genius who invented Magic: The Gathering.  So when it came out there was a literal frenzy.  While I really like this game, but in all honesty almost gave it 4 stars because simply because I didn\'t completely feel it lived up to the hype.\r\n\r\nThat said, I need to judge a game on it\'s own merit, and for a game whose action is primarily dice rolling, this game is a lot of fun.  The theme is fantastic, as who doesn\'t like the idea of being a huge monster trying to take over Tokyo.\r\n\r\nI think the reason I just had to give this game 5 stars is not only because it is fun, but it is a game that anybody can play.  Concidering the level of sophistication this game brings to the table, that is saying a lot.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(202,2607,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 08:56:48','2016-08-24 15:56:48','This is a solid game that I would say is better for a family gathering than it is for parties.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(203,2596,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:04:23','2016-08-24 16:04:23','It\'s Uno, not sure what needs said about this game.  It reminds me of rainy days and camping with my family as a kid.  Kinda crazy how such a simple game can bring so many good times.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(204,2527,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:11:03','2016-08-24 16:11:03','I love any game that challenges you to think, but is easy to play, and this game absolutely nailed it!  I don\'t think such a simple game has gotten so many raving reviews as this one has.  The bottom line is that it is just a good old fashioned fun game!\r\n\r\nPlayers need to work together in teams of 2 or 4 to play spy\'s trying to reveal their operatives.  It takes a lot of creativity to come up with clues that not only help your teammates, but don\'t end up giving them the wrong ideas.  Choose the wrong character and you\'re done!\r\n\r\nFor me the ultimate test for a game is what my dad will think of it.  He loves playing games but hates complicated rules.  He absolutely LOVED this game.\r\n\r\nIf you haven\'t played CodeNames I would say this is one that should DEFINITELY be on your shelf.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(205,2589,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:12:48','2016-08-24 16:12:48','Sequence is a classic.  It makes you think, but yet doesn\'t stress you out with complicated rules.  5 stars for sure.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(206,2566,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:18:17','2016-08-24 16:18:17','The hip bones connected to the... \r\n\r\nWhy do I give the most basic kids game in the world 5 stars?  Well, because still to this day I cannot master it for the life of me!  I don\'t know of another game that puts you on more pins and needs than Operation.  \r\n\r\nJust the fact that the feedback loop on screwing up is immediate is genius in my book.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(207,2576,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:19:04','2016-08-24 16:19:04','OK, so you’re probably not going to be captivated by the game itself. That said, the fun part about this game as an old person isn’t the game itself. The fun part is the joy you see on the little ones face as you slide down a chute, putting you further behind than they are. There is a reason that this game has been a best-seller for so many years and I think the new artwork is really nice.\r\n\r\nAll that said, its still not as cool as CandyLand.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(208,2492,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:21:00','2016-08-24 16:21:00','Great game.  Simple, yet requires a little bit of strategy and memory.  Our family had a ton of fun with it.  \r\n\r\nI really think they nailed it with the packaging too.  The pouch is great for travel and has people intrigued as you pull the game out.\r\n\r\nOnly critique is that players are eliminated from rounds.  That said, it is only for a few minutes.  If you don\'t have it you should add it to your collection.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(209,2496,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:22:34','2016-08-24 16:22:34','I think this game is fun because the entire point is to bamboozle the other players.  Any game where lying is mandatory makes for a pretty interesting time.  \r\n\r\nI think my favorite part of this game is the art.  That, and the fact that it is really easy to play.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(210,2667,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:25:20','2016-08-24 16:25:20','At first I was like \"these guys ripped off Cards Against Humanity, that ain\'t cool\".  Then I thought about the fact that CAH is the same exact gameplay as Apples to Apples and I thought it was only fitting.\r\n\r\nIn regard to the quality of the game itself, if you like CAH you will like this.  If you haven\'t played it, you will love it, assuming you are NOT easily offended.\r\n\r\nIf rude, crude and down right nasty things don\'t bother you, then this is a great way to spend a Friday night with friends.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(211,2612,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:27:38','2016-08-24 16:27:38','The best word I can use to describe this game is BEAUTIFUL.\r\n\r\nThe premise is really cool, you are a traveler on a great journey.  I seriously think the different ways to earn points along the way is nothing short of genius.\r\n\r\nThe art work and graphic design on this game really do enhance it.  It just feels good.\r\n\r\nIt takes a few minutes to learn, but one of those that are really easy once you get going.\r\n\r\nIt is one of the top 10 games I recommend to people.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(212,2550,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:29:17','2016-08-24 16:29:17','This game is as fun as the people you are with.  I love it because it takes up no space (can be carried in your pocket or purse) and it is never the same game twice.  It is all about creativity and imagination, making it not only a great game for grown ups, but for kids as well.   With the price being as low as it is, I HIGHLY recommend it.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(213,2605,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:34:15','2016-08-24 16:34:15','This is an ALL-TIME favorite at our house over the holidays.  We seriously cannot get enough Wits and Wagers!\r\n\r\nWhile there is a trivia component, it is not actual trivia as much as it is guesstimating.  All the questions are number based, so you just write down your best guess.  This alone makes for absolute hilarity!  \r\n\r\nFor example, the question \"when was the first issue of Superman comic published\" got an answer of 1768.  While I won\'t name names, we got so many laughs about the idea of Superman being published before the Declaration of Independance.\r\n\r\nThe best part of the game though is the betting.  It is genius how it is laid out, with the answers that were on the high end or the low end paying higher odds.  We just love this game.\r\n\r\nIt is worth noting that we\'ve purchased several versions of this game over the years, and have noticed that they have changed the scoring several times.  After a few adjustments, they have got it PERFECT now.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(214,2515,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:35:17','2016-08-24 16:35:17','This is a game that many people love and I thought was pretty cool.  It is especially good for those of us that grew up in the 8-bit Nintendo world.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(215,2564,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:37:02','2016-08-24 16:37:02','Any game that makes you use your noodle like this and people still love must be pretty awesome.  I am personally the worst at it, but I can\'t blame the game for my lack of proper vocabulary.  That ain\'t fair.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(216,2570,'matt','matt@boardgames.com','','162.193.81.212','2016-08-24 09:38:37','2016-08-24 16:38:37','This game is obviously a classic and as a kid I absolutely loved it.  Think I had a special place in my heart for this when I was young as my dad was actually on a battleship when in the Navy.  The new art work is pretty awesome.',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.11; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0','',0,7),(224,2517,'danny','danny@boardgames.com','','96.38.162.80','2016-08-24 14:08:13','2016-08-24 21:08:13','One of my favorite games hands down! Typically I lean towards liking the more intense strategy games but this game has the perfect blend of casual fun and strategy to make this game instantly re-playable once you finish a game! The game starts off light and easy but as the rounds progress things get more and more intense as you try to be the last boat standing without being eaten by the dragons that move across the board.\r\n\r\nThere\'s nothing quite like the feeling when the stars align and you play your tiles just right so that one of your friends has no choice but to rush straight to the devouring maws of a boat hungry dragon!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,8),(225,2615,'danny','danny@boardgames.com','','96.38.162.80','2016-08-24 14:19:50','2016-08-24 21:19:50','If I could give this game more than 5 stars I would! I wasn\'t sure what to expect the first time I played this. Zombies are everywhere these days and it\'s easy to think that people are just trying to cash in on the genre, but oh man, this takes things to a whole other level. \r\n\r\nThis game takes the zombie survival genre up a notch. Not only does it bring you the bleak realization that at any second the zombie horde will ravage your small shanty town settlement. That as the survivors in your community perish the zombie horde only grows stronger. That as your community grows, the problems grow. This game takes into account so many of the real life survival factors that would actually present themselves if this situation happened in real life.\r\n\r\nTaking all of that into account the game sounds great already, but each player has their own secret objective to win and it\'s possible that one of the players is up to no good and their winning objective involves traitorous sabotage. So as you\'re working together in co-op mode to save your settlement, the constant worry that one of your comrades may be actively working against you is constantly in the back of your mind. So much fun!\r\n\r\nThe last time I played this game my character was actually the traitor. The twisted tale I wove to get my fellow players to turn against each other was beautiful in its machinations. Ah, such a good time!',0,'1','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Safari/537.36','',0,8),(226,3390,'WooCommerce','woocommerce@boardgames.com','','','2016-08-24 16:48:29','2016-08-24 23:48:29','Items shipped via UPS on August 24, 2016 with tr