-27 09:24:09','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/aquarius_medium.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(561,1,'2016-04-27 09:24:10','2016-04-27 09:24:10','','arcanewonders_medium','','inherit','open','closed','','arcanewonders_medium','','','2016-04-27 09:24:10','2016-04-27 09:24:10','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/arcanewonders_medium.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(562,1,'2016-04-27 09:24:10','2016-04-27 09:24:10','','ares','','inherit','open','closed','','ares','','','2016-04-27 09:24:10','2016-04-27 09:24:10','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/ares.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(563,1,'2016-04-27 09:24:11','2016-04-27 09:24:11','','asmadigames_medium','','inherit','open','closed','','asmadigames_medium','','','2016-04-27 09:24:11','2016-04-27 09:24:11','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/asmadigames_medium.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(564,1,'2016-04-27 09:24:11','2016-04-27 09:24:11','','asmodee_medium','','inherit','open','closed','','asmodee_medium','','','2016-04-27 09:24:11','2016-04-27 09:24:11','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/asmodee_medium.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(565,1,'2016-04-27 09:24:12','2016-04-27 09:24:12','','atlasgames_medium','','inherit','open','closed','','atlasgames_medium','','','2016-04-27 09:24:12','2016-04-27 09:24:12','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/atlasgames_medium.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(572,1,'2016-05-01 01:33:15','2016-05-01 01:33:15','','index','','inherit','open','closed','','index','','','2016-05-01 01:33:15','2016-05-01 01:33:15','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/index.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(573,1,'2016-05-01 01:33:15','2016-05-01 01:33:15','','slider-2','','inherit','open','closed','','slider-2','','','2016-05-01 01:33:15','2016-05-01 01:33:15','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/slider-2.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(574,1,'2016-05-01 01:33:16','2016-05-01 01:33:16','','slider-3','','inherit','open','closed','','slider-3','','','2016-05-01 01:33:16','2016-05-01 01:33:16','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/slider-3.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(578,1,'2016-05-01 01:46:05','2016-05-01 01:46:05','','secure_payments','','inherit','open','closed','','secure_payments','','','2016-05-01 01:46:05','2016-05-01 01:46:05','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/secure_payments.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(579,1,'2016-05-01 02:07:43','2016-05-01 02:07:43','','bg-weekly','','inherit','open','closed','','bg-weekly','','','2016-05-01 02:07:43','2016-05-01 02:07:43','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/bg-weekly.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(582,1,'2016-05-02 23:44:43','2016-05-02 23:44:43','','bg-points','','inherit','open','closed','','bg-points','','','2016-05-02 23:44:43','2016-05-02 23:44:43','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/bg-points.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(583,1,'2016-05-02 23:44:43','2016-05-02 23:44:43','','bg-weekly','','inherit','open','closed','','bg-weekly-2','','','2016-05-02 23:44:43','2016-05-02 23:44:43','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/bg-weekly.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(584,1,'2016-05-03 00:05:43','2016-05-03 00:05:43','','bg-blog','','inherit','open','closed','','bg-blog','','','2016-05-03 00:05:43','2016-05-03 00:05:43','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/bg-blog.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(585,2,'2016-05-03 00:13:13','2016-05-03 00:13:13','','Board Game Blog','','publish','closed','closed','','blog','','','2016-08-05 04:44:24','2016-08-05 04:44:24','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/?page_id=585',0,'page','',0),(937,6,'2016-02-02 01:03:40','2016-02-02 01:03:40','It can be tricky finding a game that is appropriate to play for all ages. The two biggest concerns are the maturity of the content and the complexity of the gameplay. If you are going to be playing with kids or young adults it is important to be aware of these aspects of the games you will be playing. It isn\'t difficult to determine if content wise a game is suited for children, the complexity of gameplay is another story.\r\n\r\nYou want to be confident that a child will be able to comprehend the mechanics and objectives while at the same time not be so rudimentary that an adult wouldn\'t enjoy the experience. Below are a few games that should provide sufficient entertainment value while being accessible enough for a kid to pick up.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2983\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Catan-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Catan_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n<strong>Catan</strong>\r\n\r\nCatan is a fun strategy game with an element of chance, providing quite a bit of replay value. Players gain points by building settlements, cities and roads. Building settlements and cities require resources gathered and traded for, and players must be wary of the Robber who can steal you resources.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2984\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Ticket-To-Ride-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Ticket To Ride_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n<strong>Ticket To Ride</strong>\r\n\r\nTicket To Ride has simple gameplay that is easy to pick up, but there is enough strategy to keep it interesting. The objective of the game is to gain the most points by connecting routes (the longer the route, the most points gained), fulfilling destination tickets and building the longest route. Players also must actively prevent the other players from reaching these objectives.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/apples-to-apples/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2981\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Apples-To-Apples-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Apples To Apples_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/apples-to-apples/\"><strong>Apples To Apples</strong></a>\r\n\r\nApples to Apples is a party game for the whole family. Players are dealt red cards which have a noun printed on them. The judge (each round a new player is the judge) draws a green card which has an adjective printed on it. The green card is displayed for all players to see. Each player then chooses which of their red cards is the best companion to the green card. The Judge then decides which red card they like best.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2955\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/takenoko-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"takenoko_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n<strong>Takenoko</strong>\r\n\r\nIn Takenoko your objective is to cultivate a parcel of land for growing Bamboo. It is a game of balancing feeding your Bamboo Pandas and farming the parcels all the while completing objectives. The game ends when a player completes 7 or 9 objectives (depending on the number of players). It doesn\'t get much cuter than Pandas eating all your bamboo. This one is quick to learn and fun to boot.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/castle-panic/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2982\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Castle-Panic-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Castle Panic_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/castle-panic/\"><strong>Castle Panic</strong></a>\r\n\r\nCastle Panic is a co-op tower defense game. Players must work together to defend the Castle (situated at the center of the board) from Monsters attacking from the forest. Players win or lose together but the player with the most victory points is crowned the Master Slayer.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Board Games Fun For All Ages','','publish','open','open','','board-games-fun-for-all-ages','','','2016-08-23 20:26:42','2016-08-24 03:26:42','',0,'http://secretboardgames.com/?p=937',0,'post','',0),(1522,6,'2016-03-09 06:18:45','2016-03-09 06:18:45','It can be tricky figuring out what kind of game is appropriate for what situation. Obviously it’s probably not the best idea to bust out Cards Against Humanity at your Grandma’s birthday.\r\n\r\nBut mostly it’s not that cut and dry when deciding on a board game for a given scenario. Below is a list compiled for a few games to try out when you find yourself in a spot with specific parameters.\r\n\r\nNow, your mileage may vary (we’re all snowflakes right?) but this list should be a decent guideline to get you pointed in the right direction.\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 30px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">YOU ONLY HAVE A FEW MINUTES</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>1. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/love-letter/\">Love Letter</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/love-letter/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2974\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Love-Letter-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Love Letter\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Love Letter is a card game of deduction, risk and a bit of luck. Good for 2-4 players and each game lasts about 15 minutes. The entire game is only 20 cards so it’s also a good one to play on the go.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>2. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/sushi-go/\">Sushi Go!</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/sushi-go/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2947\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Sushi-Go-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Sushi Go_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Sushi Go is a fast paced game where the objective is to snag the best Sushi combo and pass the junk to the other players. You get points for making the most Maki rolls and collecting a full set of Sashimi. You also need to accommodate for dessert. Gather the most points to win. A game for 2-5 players and lasts about 15 minutes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>3. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/coup/\">Coup</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/coup/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2972\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Coup-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Coup\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Coup is a game of bluffing, to win you need to have the most influence. Players start the game with two coins and two influence cards (character cards) face down. Your objective is to lessen your opponents’ influence through actions that force them to reveal their face down character cards, while at the same time maintaining your influence by preventing your character cards from being revealed. For 2-6 players, games last about 15 minutes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 30px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">FAMILY GET-TOGETHER</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>1. Scattergories</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2978\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Scattergories-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Scattergories\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">A Party game where teams come up with answers that fit categories listed on their cards. The catch is answers need to begin with the letter determined by a die roll and answers must be unique, no points are awarded if another team provides the same answer as you. Come up with as many answers before time runs out. The team with the most points wins.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>2. R<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/rorys-story-cubes/\">ory\'s Story Cubes</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/rorys-story-cubes/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2977\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Rorys-Story-Cubes-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Rory\'s Story Cubes\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">The objective here is to create a creative story. There are 9 six sided ‘cubes’, each side with a picture. Your job is to generate a story inspired by the pictures presented after rolling the cubes. You can add complexity by creating cooperative stories (each player contributing) or by implementing a point system. A fun, quick and simple game for any number of players.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>3. Blokus</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2970\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Blokus-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Blokus\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Blokus is a fast paced strategy game. Each player starts with 21 game pieces and the objective is to place all of them on the board before your opponents. But each piece placed must touch another piece of the same color, and must only be touching at the corner. Simple to learn but complex to play, good for the whole family.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 30px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">YOU’RE DRUNK AND SO IS EVERYONE ELSE</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>1. Cards Against Humanity</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2971\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Cards-Against-Humanity-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Cards Against Humanity\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Have you ever tried playing CAH sober? Yeah me neither. Two drinks deep is basically a prerequisite for having a good time with this one. The premise of the game is simple (and awful) – One player plays a prompt card and the other players play the most ‘appropriate’ response card to compliment the prompt. Points don’t matter and the more horrible your response generally the better.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>2. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/one-night-ultimate-werewolf/\">One Night Ultimate Werewolf</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/one-night-ultimate-werewolf/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2976\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/One-Night-Ultimate-Werewolf-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"One Night Ultimate Werewolf\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">One Night Ultimate Werewolf is a fast-paced game where everyone plays a different role. In the course of only one night and the following morning, the players will determine who among them is a werewolf…hopefully. This is a game of deception and deduction. Each game only lasts a few minutes which is a bonus because you’re drunk and aren’t paying attention anyway.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>3. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/sheriff-of-nottingham/\">Sheriff of Nottingham</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/sheriff-of-nottingham/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2979\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Sheriff-of-Nottingham-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Sheriff of Nottingham\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Sheriff is a game of bluffing, bribery and negotiation. Players take turns playing the role of the Sheriff while the other players are merchants. Merchants are attempting to bring goods into the city for profit, the Sheriff’s role is to catch merchants smuggling contraband into the city.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">This is a game perfect for role-playing and how better to role-play a medieval sheriff or merchant than by being totally lit? Win the game by having the most money by smuggling the most contraband, accepting the most bribes or by being an honest merchant.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 30px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">YOU AND YOUR FRIENDS ARE UNEMPLOYED</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>1. Mage Knight</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2975\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Mage-Knight-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Mage Knight\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Mage Knight is a game of Epic Exploration and Conquest that mixes character development, intrigue, and the clashing of swords.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">This a dense, complex and long game – it’s part random tile exploration, part deck building, part dice rolling. A mishmash of fantasy excellence. But it’s long. And requires a healthy bout of stamina to complete. Did I mention it’s long? You’ll need a day to play it. Literally.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>2. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/diplomacy/\">Diplomacy</a></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/diplomacy/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2973\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Diplomacy-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Diplomacy\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">The Grand Poobah game of intrigue, cunning and negotiation. The strategy game to beat all strategy games. The objective is to expand your empire over pre-World War 1 Europe through any means necessary, usually by building alliances with other players then back stabbing them.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Generally not recommended to be played with friends whom you want to keep as friends. Play time listed on the box is 360 minutes which is an optimistic approximation.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><strong>3. Arkham Horror</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2969\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Arkham-Horror-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Arkham Horror\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 60px;\">Are you a fan of the Cthulhu Mythos, co-op games and have six hours to kill? This is the game for you. Players can select from 16 unique playable investigator characters, each with unique abilities, and will square off against the diabolical servants of 8 Ancient Ones, including Ithaqua, Hastur, and the terrible Cthulhu!</p>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nDo you have any suggestions for the perfect game for the perfect situation? Let us know in the comments below!\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','A Board Game For Almost Any Situation','','publish','open','open','','a-board-game-for-almost-any-situation','','','2016-08-23 20:25:31','2016-08-24 03:25:31','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1522',0,'post','',0),(1525,6,'2016-03-09 06:35:58','2016-03-09 06:35:58','What is so appealing about acting like a kid? Well, kids are confident and carefree. So there’s that. They also view the world through an unfiltered lens, they have empathy and are brimming with curiosity.\r\n\r\nKids aren’t overly concerned with structure, they’re easily distracted and embrace the nonsensical. Kid life is a microcosm of the base reality of our universe. In a word – chaotic. As such the best games for recapturing that state of existence, for a time anyway, are games that embrace chaos and absurdism.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Cash N Guns</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2964\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Cash-and-Guns-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Cash and Guns_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\nThe set up for Cash and Guns is fairly simple – Players are a gang of robbers who have just completed a heist and now it’s time to divvy up the goods. The problem is how to split the loot – everyone wants the biggest piece of the pie! Out come the guns and negotiations begin.\r\n\r\nEach round players secretly load their guns, either with a Bang! card or a Click! card and aim at another player. At the count of three cards are revealed – if you’re hit with a Bang! card you gain a wound, everyone else gets to pick a piece of loot. After eight rounds the game ends, whoever is still alive and has the most loot wins. Cash and Guns is a game of bluffing, intimidation and luck.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Exploding Kittens</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2966\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Exploding-Kittens-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Exploding Kittens_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\nExploding Kittens is an elimination card game not too unlike Russian Roulette. Notable exceptions are you don’t play it in a Gulag and employing a .38 Special is frowned upon.\r\n\r\nThe basic gist of the game is you draw cards until you draw an exploding kitten at which point you explode and lose. There is one fewer exploding kitten card in the deck than players participating and there are cards to mitigate drawing an exploding kitten. But really, you’re most likely to explode at some point.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/epic-spell-wars-of-the-battle-wizards-duel-at-mt-skullzfyre/\">Epic Spell Wars</a></strong>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/epic-spell-wars-of-the-battle-wizards-duel-at-mt-skullzfyre/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2965\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Epic-Spell-Wars-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Epic Spell Wars_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nYou are a Battle Wizard vying to be the last wizard standing. Create unique, powerful and devastating spells by combining up to three spell components then fling them at your enemies.\r\n\r\nYou can also augment your spells with Arcane Artifacts to make them even more brutal. But beware – your spells might melt the face of your opponent or they may blow up in your lap. Epic Spell Wars is hilarious, quick to learn and has a lot of replay value.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/fluxx/\">Fluxx</a></strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/fluxx/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2967\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Fluxx-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Fluxx_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nFluxx is the epitome of chaos. The game begins simply enough – each player draws a card and plays a card. Then madness ensues. There are four card types – Keeper, Goal, New Rule and Action.\r\n\r\nKeeper cards are generally the cards required to win the game. Goal cards change the win conditions for the game. New Rule cards, you may have guessed, add a new rule – how many cards to draw and how many to play each round for example. Action cards add even more chaos to the game by forcing players to switch cards with one another, shuffle cards into the deck, eliminate a New Rule, etc.\r\n\r\nFluxx is aptly named and a fun, quick game.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. We Didn\'t Playtest This At All</strong>\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2968\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/We-Didnt-Playtest-This-at-All-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"We Didn\'t Playtest This at All_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\nBasically Fluxx on steroids. At the start of the game every play draws two cards from the deck and then determine who goes first. That player then draws another card from the deck and decides which card they want to play.\r\n\r\nFrom there every player draws one card and plays one card on their turn. It sounds pretty normal right? Well it’s not. Be ready for Dragons, Black Holes, Rock Paper Scissors battles, Dinosaurs, Zombies and Bananas. Each game last under five minutes and is jam packed with chaos, weirdness and fun.','Games To Unleash Your Inner Kid','','publish','open','open','','games-to-unleash-your-inner-kid','','','2016-08-23 20:21:07','2016-08-24 03:21:07','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1525',0,'post','',0),(1577,6,'2016-04-13 00:19:25','2016-04-13 00:19:25','Being a new gamer can be intimidating and overwhelming. There are so many board games with dozens of components, complex rulesets, deep strategy and more. It can be stressful playing these games, especially with folks who are familiar with the games. The objective to playing board games is to have fun, not be stressed out! Below are a list of games that are extraordinarily easy to learn but still contain a lot of depth.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2962\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Splendor-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"Splendor_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n1.) Splendor\r\n\r\nSplendor is a board game of gathering Chips and purchasing Development cards to gain Prestige. Players can perform one action each turn - gather Chips, purchase a Development card or reserve a card. The correct Chips must be gathered to purchase a Development card, and the Chips become rarer as the game progresses while the Developent cards become more expensive. Development cards provide Prestige, and the first player to 15 Prestige wins.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/star-realms-colony-wars/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2963\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/star-realms-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"star realms_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n2.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/star-realms-colony-wars/\">Star Realms!</a>\r\n\r\nStar Realms is a 2 player space battle themed deck builder that can be learned in about 15 minutes. Each player begins with the game with the same cards in their deck - two Viper cards (attack), eight Scout cards (purchasing) as well as 50 Authority (life). Use Scouts to purchase Ships and Bases from Trade Row to improve your attacks, defenses and abilities. Use Vipers and other ships to attack the other player, the objective is to reduce your opponent to zero Authority. Each game lasts 20 minutes or so.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/dominion/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2957\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/dominion-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"dominion_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n3.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/dominion/\">Dominion</a>\r\n\r\nDominion is a medieval themed deck builder. Each player has their own deck of cards they draw from. Players use their cards to perform actions and buy cards from a common pool of card stacks, including Action, Treasure, and Victory cards. The objective is to have the most Victory Points at the end of the game.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2959\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/hive-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"hive_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n4.) Hive\r\n\r\nHive is a tile based board game of bugs and bees. There is no actual board. The pieces are added to the playing area thus creating the board. As more and more pieces are added the game becomes a fight to see who can be the first to capture the opposing Queen Bee.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/power-grid/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2960\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/power-grid-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"power grid_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n5.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/power-grid/\">Power Grid</a>\r\n\r\nPower Grid is a board game where each player owns power plants and tries to supply electricity to cities. During the game the players will bid on power plants and buy resources to produce electricity in their effort to provide power to a growing number of cities. The player who provides power to the most cities wins.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2958\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/five-tribes-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"five tribes_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n6.) Five Tribes\r\n\r\nFive Tribes is a worker placement board game. Players score by carefully maneuvering the Five Tribes of Maples over the tiles that make up the ancient city-state of the Sultanate of Naqala. Strategic movements are necessary to yield players the best advantage and their opponents the greatest disadvantage.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Fun Board Games that are Easy to Learn','','publish','open','open','','fun-board-games-that-are-easy-to-learn','','','2016-08-23 20:17:34','2016-08-24 03:17:34','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1577',0,'post','',0),(1583,6,'2016-04-13 00:24:57','2016-04-13 00:24:57','If you\'re new to board games, or just looking to improve your game playing prowess below are a handful of great, entry level games. These board games have a low barrier to entry, have great depth and strategy without being overly complex. Perfect for improving your strategic chops!\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/carcassonne/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2953\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/carcassonne-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"carcassonne_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n1.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/carcassonne/\">Carcassonne</a>\r\n\r\nCarcassonne is a clever tile-laying game. The southern French city of Carcassonne is famous for its unique roman and medieval fortifications. The players develop the area around Carcassonne and deploy their followers on the roads, in the cities, in the cloisters, and in the fields. The skill of the players to develop the area will determine who is victorious.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2954\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/small-world-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"small world_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n2.) Small World\r\n\r\nSmall World is a zany, light-hearted civilization game in which 2-5 players vie for conquest and control of a board that is simply too small to accommodate them all. Picking the right combination of fantasy races and unique special powers, players must rush to expand their empires - often at the expense of weaker neighbors. Yet they must also know when to push their own over-extended civilization into decline and ride a new one to victory.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2955\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/takenoko-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"takenoko_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n3.) Takenoko\r\n\r\nTakenoko is a board game with Pandas! Players need to farm parcels of land, irrigate them, and have green, yellow or pink bamboo grow. In turn, they see what the weather brings and perform two actions from among those offered to them: get a new plot of land or irrigation channel, grow bamboo, feed the panda or draw an objective card. The game ends when a player has completed 7 to 9 objectives.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/tikal/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2956\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/tikal-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"tikal_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n4.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/tikal/\">Tikal</a>\r\n\r\nTikal is a board game where players are adventurers exploring parts of a Central American jungle in search of artifacts and temples. Players gain points for recovered treasure and for temples controlled. But, both temples and treasures can change hands. The expedition that earns the most points exploring Tikal wins the game.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2952\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/7-Wonders-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"7 Wonders_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n5.) 7 Wonders\r\n\r\n7 Wonders is a card drafting game. Players portray a leader of one of the seven great cities of the Ancient World. Over the course of Three Ages players must fortify their defenses, gather resources and build structures.  At the end of the third age victory points are tallied and the player with the most points wins.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;','Best Strategy Games for Non-Hardcore Gamers','','publish','open','open','','best-strategy-games-for-non-hardcore-gamers','','','2016-08-23 20:15:28','2016-08-24 03:15:28','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1583',0,'post','',0),(1586,6,'2016-04-13 00:30:49','2016-04-13 00:30:49','Game night is a great way to come together, interact and bond with family. A problem that may arise is your current go to games could become stale due to overplay. If you\'re on the look out for a new family board game on a budget look no further! Below are a handful of great games for all ages, each for under $25.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/hanabi/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2946\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/hanabi-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"hanabi_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n1.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/hanabi/\">Hanabi</a>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nHanabi is a co-operative deduction card game. Players work together to create the most spectacular fireworks show by playing specific cards in the correct order. The twist is players cannot see their own cards, only the cards of the other players. Each game last about 20 minutes and the MSRP is $11.\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2942\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/bang-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"bang_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\n2.) Bang!\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nBang! is a wild west themed card game where players participate in a good old fashioned shoot-out. Players are randomly assigned one of four available character type cards which determines their abilities and establishes their win condition. The four character types are Sheriff, Deputy, Outlaw and Renegade; all roles except the Sheriff\'s are secret.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/wits-and-wagers/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2948\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/wits-and-wagers-family-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"wits and wagers family_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n3.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/wits-and-wagers/\">Wits and Wagers Family</a>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nWits and Wagers Family is a trivia party game. First, everyone writes down a guess to a fun question like “How many people have walked on the moon?” Then players try to score points by choosing which guess is closest to the right answer. With simpler rules and all new family-friendly questions, the Family Edition is the game that kids and parents actually enjoy playing together!\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/forbidden-island/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2945\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/forbidden-island-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"forbidden island_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n4.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/forbidden-island/\">Forbidden Island</a>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nForbidden Island is a co-operative adventuring and survival board game. Players are a team of fearless adventurers on a do-or-die mission to capture four sacred treasures from the ruins of a perilous paradise. Players have to work together and make some pulse-pounding maneuvers, as the island will sink beneath every step! Race to collect the treasures and make a triumphant escape before you are swallowed into the watery abyss!\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/zombie-dice/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2949\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/zombie-dice-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"zombie dice_blog\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\n5.) <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/zombie-dice/\">Zombie Dice</a>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nZombie Dice is a quick dice game for any zombie fan (or the whole zombie family). The 13 custom dice are your victims. Push your luck to eat their brains, but stop before the shotgun blasts end your turn! Fast to learn, games are 15 minutes or less to play.','Best Family Board Games for Under $25','','publish','open','open','','best-family-board-games-for-under-25','','','2016-08-23 15:52:59','2016-08-23 22:52:59','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1586',0,'post','',2),(1597,6,'2016-04-20 01:44:08','2016-04-20 01:44:08','There are a number of places where you can play Board Games online, right in your web browser. One of the most popular of those sites being <a href=\"http://en.boardgamearena.com/\">Board Game Arena</a> which is free, you simply need to register to play. Online board gaming is a growing trend, for good reason - it\'s convenient, readily accessible and doesn\'t require a huge time investment. It\'s also a good way to try out a game before you make a purchase.\r\n\r\nAnother, even more convenient, way to play board games online is via mobile apps on your phone or tablet. On mobile board games are literally at your fingertips - you can play them during a break at work, while travelling or when you\'re on the commode.\r\n\r\nOnline Board Games and Mobile Apps don\'t provide the same experience as a tabletop session with friends and family, but they\'re a great way to scratch that proverbial board gaming itch between Game Nights.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/boss-monster/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2936\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/boss-monsterblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"boss monster(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nBoss Monster. Android - Free, iOS - Free\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/boss-monster/\">Boss Monster</a> is a dungeon-building card game that challenges players to become the ultimate villains: video game bosses. Thousands of players around the world have enjoyed the paper version of the game, but now Brotherwise Games has partnered with video game developer Plain Concepts, creators of Wave Engine, to bring Boss Monster from the tabletop to the digital world!\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/carcassonne/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2937\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/carcassonneblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"carcassonne(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nCarcassonne. Android - $4.99, iOS - $9.99\r\n\r\nThe award-winning tile based board game is finally here on Android! Just a few years after its release, <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/carcassonne/\">Carcassonne</a> became a modern classic and a must-play. Turn by turn, the players create a landscape by placing tiles with roads, cities, fields, and cloisters. The players deploy their followers, so called \"Meeples\", as knights, monks, thieves, or farmers to earn points. The player with the most points after the final scoring wins the game. The ever-changing landscape makes each game a new experience. You can play against clever AI opponents or with up to 5 other players in an online or local multiplayer match.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2938\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/catanblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"catan(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\nCatan. Android - $3.99, iOS - $4.99\r\n\r\n\"Catan\", the legendary strategy game provides gaming fun anytime, anywhere.\r\nTrue to the original game, you can compete with up to four players for the most settlements, the longest roads and the largest army. You can trade with each other and claim the precious land with all its resources.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/diplomacy/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2939\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/diplomacyblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"diplomacy(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nDiplomacy (droidippy). Android - Free, iOS - Free\r\n\r\nDroidippy is a <a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/diplomacy/\">Diplomacy</a> like game running on devices compatible with Android 2.2 and having at least one Google account.\r\n\r\nIf you have never played Diplomacy it could perhaps be explained as being a mix of Risk, Poker, Chess and Rock-Paper-Scissors. It was supposedly the favorite game of John Kennedy and Henry Kissinger.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/star-realms-colony-wars/\"><img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2940\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/star-realmsblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"star realms(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" /></a>\r\n\r\nStar Realms!. Android - Free, iOS - Free\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://boardgames.com/buy/star-realms-colony-wars/\">Star Realms</a> combines addictive Deckbuilding Game play with exciting Trading Card Game style combat!\r\n\r\nDesigned by Magic Hall of Famers Darwin Kastle and Rob Dougherty (of the Ascension Deckbuilding Game), Star Realms’ amazingly rich yet easy to learn game play will provide endless hours of entertainment.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-thumbnail wp-image-2941\" src=\"https://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/ticket-to-rideblog-150x150.png\" alt=\"ticket to ride(blog)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" />\r\n\r\nTicket To Ride. Android - $6.99, iOS - $6.99\r\n\r\nTicket to Ride takes less than one minute to learn but a lifetime to master. Over 48 million games played online and a new game starting every 4 seconds on average! In addition to the exciting cross-platform asynchronous multiplayer mode, players will enjoy a new intuitive user interface, new social media capabilities to share exciting moments, and the brand new India map, the first vertical map to be available on Ticket to Ride.','Playing Board Games Online','','publish','open','open','','playing-board-games-online','','','2016-08-23 15:49:27','2016-08-23 22:49:27','',0,'https://secretboardgames.com/?p=1597',0,'post','',0),(1608,1,'2016-05-15 17:15:08','2016-05-15 17:15:08','','pawn','','inherit','open','closed','','pawn','','','2016-05-15 17:15:08','2016-05-15 17:15:08','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/pawn.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(1617,2,'2016-05-25 04:40:04','2016-05-25 04:40:04','','dontbealoser','','inherit','open','closed','','dontbealoser','','','2016-07-22 12:40:02','2016-07-22 12:40:02','',272,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dontbealoser.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(1625,2,'2016-05-25 20:57:57','2016-05-25 20:57:57','<div class=\"one-fourth\">[cmk_menu menu=\"Affiliate Menu\" container_class=\"block\"]</div>\r\n<div class=\"three-fourths last\">\r\n<h2 class=\"bord\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\">Affiliate Program:</span></h2>\r\n<strong>SIGN UP. LINK TO BOARDGAMES.COM. MAKE MONEY.</strong>\r\n\r\nWant to become part of the BG inner circle and make money while you’re at it? Join our affiliate program and earn referral commissions by sending customers to our site. It’s simple to do and it’s free! Getting started is easy, just follow these steps:\r\n\r\n<strong>Getting Started</strong>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>Sign up to be a part of the program.</li>\r\n 	<li>Link to Boardgames.com from your web site.</li>\r\n 	<li>Earn commissions of up to 9% from all qualified sales that came from your site.</li>\r\n 	<li>Sit back and rake in the profits!</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<strong>How Does it work?</strong>\r\n\r\nAfter signing up to be part of the program, you link to our site from yours. The links contain a special tracking code, and when customers click on those links and purchase through us, you earn a commission (up to 9%!) on every item they purchase.\r\n\r\nIt couldn’t be simpler! We’ve streamlined our entire Promo Team affiliate process to ensure ease of use, while still maintaining extremely accurate tracking methods.\r\n\r\n<strong>How do I get started?</strong>\r\n\r\nSign up to be part of the program. We manually review all applications within 3 business days. Once your application is approved, you will receive an e-mail with instructions on what you need to do to get going and start earning money!\r\n\r\n<strong>How do I get more information?</strong>\r\n\r\nCheck out our FAQ for more info about our affiliate program, including detailed information about getting started, tips on making your program a success, and information about what we are doing to make our affiliate program successful for you – including our promise to communicate regularly with our affiliates.\r\n\r\nRead our Frequently Asked Questions for more.\r\n\r\nReal-Time Statistics and Reports:\r\n\r\nLog in anytime to check your performance with data of sales, traffic generated and your commission balance!\r\n\r\nRules and Requirements:\r\n\r\nWe do have some basic ground rules for the program, so please read before signing up.\r\n\r\nClick here for full program rules.\r\n\r\n<a class=\"btn green\" href=\"#\">Start Earning Commission &gt;&gt;</a>\r\n\r\n</div>','Affiliate Program','','publish','closed','closed','','affiliate-program','','','2016-08-05 05:08:25','2016-08-05 05:08:25','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/?page_id=1625',0,'page','',0),(1654,2,'2016-05-25 21:21:07','2016-05-25 21:21:07','<div class=\"one-fourth\">[cmk_menu menu=\"Content Menu\" container_class=\"block\"]</div>\r\n<div class=\"two-fourths right\">\r\n\r\n<img class=\"alignnone wp-image-1655 size-full\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/BGweeklylogo.jpg\" alt=\"BG Weekly Board Game Newsletter\" width=\"291\" height=\"94\" />\r\n<p style=\"text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 16px;\"><b>Sign up for THE exclusive boardgames.com email newsletter!</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 14px;\">BOARD GAME NEWS, Products, Content and DiscountS Galore</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Our subscribers see the newest games first, including limited-edition &amp; hard-to-keep-in-stock stuff that sells out fast.</li>\r\n 	<li>Get in on top-secret deals and discounts just for our email subscribers.</li>\r\n 	<li>We send our email newsletter once a week on Fridays.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span class=\"manual-optin-trigger btn orange\" data-optin-slug=\"pv4ng1rmqzn3mmep\">Sign me Up!</span>\r\n[brgm_fb_link]</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"one-fourth last\"><span style=\"position: absolute; width: 100%; min-height: 400px; background: #000;visibility:hidden;\">a</span></div>','Board Games Weekly','','publish','closed','closed','','board-game-information','','','2016-08-10 23:13:24','2016-08-10 23:13:24','',0,'http://boardgamesdev.wpengine.com/?page_id=1654',0,'page','',0),(1668,2,'2016-05-28 16:39:10','2016-05-28 16:39:10','<div class=\"one-fourth\">\r\n\r\n[cmk_menu menu