rash','closed','closed','','0-cartinstantbucks-10-07-16-8__trashed','','','2016-10-12 13:12:28','2016-10-12 20:12:28','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?post_type=shop_coupon&#038;p=3687',0,'shop_coupon','',0),(3689,1,'2016-10-07 12:05:42','2016-10-07 19:05:42','','Order &ndash; October 7, 2016 @ 12:05 PM','adfasdfs','wc-cancelled','open','closed','order_57f7f00016392','order-oct-07-2016-0657-pm','','','2016-10-07 12:05:42','2016-10-07 19:05:42','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=3689',0,'shop_order','',1),(3690,1,'2016-10-07 14:18:27','2016-10-07 21:18:27','','Order &ndash; October 7, 2016 @ 02:18 PM','','wc-cancelled','open','closed','order_57f80fd62249e','order-oct-07-2016-0912-pm','','','2016-10-07 14:18:27','2016-10-07 21:18:27','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=3690',0,'shop_order','',1),(3691,1,'2016-10-07 14:23:36','2016-10-07 21:23:36','','Order &ndash; October 7, 2016 @ 02:23 PM','','wc-cancelled','open','closed','order_57f8102a2602a','order-oct-07-2016-0914-pm','','','2016-10-07 14:23:36','2016-10-07 21:23:36','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?post_type=shop_order&#038;p=3691',0,'shop_order','',1),(3692,38,'2016-10-09 05:56:37','0000-00-00 00:00:00','','Auto Draft','','auto-draft','open','open','','','','','2016-10-09 05:56:37','0000-00-00 00:00:00','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?p=3692',0,'post','',0),(3693,5,'2016-10-10 11:40:46','2016-10-10 18:40:46','Get ready to be doubled over with laughter with this ridiculous mouthpiece challenge game! The Speak Out game brings friends and family together for laugh-out-loud fun as players try to say different phrases while wearing a mouthpiece that won\'t let them shut their mouth. In the Speak Out game, players draw from the deck and read the phrase as best as they can, but it\'s not so easy to do when the mouthpiece is hindering them from forming words correctly. The timer counts down as players try to say phrases such as \"he\'s my stealthy pet ferret name Garrett\", \"slow down, you careless clown\", or \"pelicans love pollywog falafels.\" The laughter continues as players try to decipher what in the world their teammate is trying to say, and must correctly guess the phrase in order to earn the card. The team with the most cards at the end of the game wins. The Speak Out game includes 200 double-sided cards, 5 mouthpieces, and a timer.\r\n\r\nHasbro gaming and all related terms are trademarks of Hasbro.\r\n<ul class=\"a-vertical a-spacing-none\">\r\n 	<li><span class=\"a-list-item\">Includes 5 mouthpieces, 200 double-sided cards, timer, and instructions</span></li>\r\n 	<li><span class=\"a-list-item\">Hilarious fun for family and friends</span></li>\r\n 	<li><span class=\"a-list-item\">Mouthpiece makes speech sound ridiculous</span></li>\r\n 	<li><span class=\"a-list-item\">Ages 16 and up</span></li>\r\n 	<li><span class=\"a-list-item\">For 4-5 players</span></li>\r\n</ul>','Speak Out','','publish','open','closed','','speak-out','','','2016-10-12 12:25:55','2016-10-12 19:25:55','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?post_type=product&#038;p=3693',0,'product','',0),(3694,5,'2016-10-10 11:45:57','2016-10-10 18:45:57','','Speak Out board game','','inherit','open','closed','','81smccklwal-_sl1500_','','','2016-10-10 11:46:07','2016-10-10 18:46:07','',3693,'https://boardgames.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/81sMCcklWAL._SL1500_.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(3695,5,'2016-10-10 11:46:11','2016-10-10 18:46:11','','516vkwkgyfl','','inherit','open','closed','','516vkwkgyfl','','','2016-10-10 11:46:11','2016-10-10 18:46:11','',3693,'https://boardgames.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/516VkWKgyfL.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(3696,5,'2016-10-10 11:46:18','2016-10-10 18:46:18','','81ok9gfratl-_sl1500_','','inherit','open','closed','','81ok9gfratl-_sl1500_','','','2016-10-10 11:46:18','2016-10-10 18:46:18','',3693,'https://boardgames.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/81ok9GFrAtL._SL1500_.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(3697,7,'2016-10-10 14:47:25','0000-00-00 00:00:00','','Auto Draft','','auto-draft','open','open','','','','','2016-10-10 14:47:25','0000-00-00 00:00:00','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?p=3697',0,'post','',0),(3698,7,'2016-10-10 14:55:08','2016-10-10 21:55:08','<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">When making the invite list for your next board game night you\'ll definitely want to keep the following players off the list...</div>\r\n<b>#1 The Rule Nazi </b>- Yes, we know that the game has rules and they are important... but these people take it to the extreme.  It\'s as if nothing makes them happier than telling you how you\'re playing the game \"ALL WRONG\".\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><iframe class=\"giphy-embed\" src=\"//giphy.com/embed/3xz2BtrwQ2wIBeciAw\" width=\"320\" height=\"200\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"> <em>No fun for you!</em></div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i><b>Solution: </b></i>Take the rule book away and feed them enough junk food to put them into a food coma\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<b>#2 The Perplexed</b> - You\'ll know this player by the constant look of confusion on their face.  It\'s not just the number of questions they ask that is annoying, its the fact that they ask the same questions over and over and over.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<iframe class=\"giphy-embed\" src=\"//giphy.com/embed/glmRyiSI3v5E4\" width=\"320\" height=\"216\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://giphy.com/gifs/glmRyiSI3v5E4\">via GIPHY</a>\r\n\r\n<i><b>Solution: </b></i>Have them play together with another player for the first game so they can learn\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<b>The Trash Talker</b> - We all love a little smack talk. In fact, it is part of what makes gaming so great.  But this is the type of person who takes being competitive way too far.  It\'s supposed to be fun, right?!\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i>Odoyle rules!</i>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div><i><b>Solution:</b></i> All players gang up on this player to make sure they never, ever win</div>\r\n<div><b>The Slow Poke</b> - There is always that one player that thinks every move through for waaaaaaaayyyy too long.  Then when they finally do take their turn you wonder what the heck they were thinking about that entire time.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div><i><b>Solution:</b></i> Agree upon a set time limit for each turn and use a timer</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div><b>The Table Flipper</b> - The most hanus of all board game ruiners are the table flippers.  We all hate to lose, but these poor sports take it to a whole new level.</div>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<div><b><i>Solution:</i></b> Super glue the table to the floor, or better yet, don\'t invite them at all!</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\nDISCLAIMER: As I write this I realize I\'m probably all of these on certain days.  Except a table flipper.  That\'s just not cool.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>IMAGE CREDIT: giphy.com</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>','5 Board Game Player Types that Ruin the Game for Everyone','','trash','open','open','','5-board-game-player-types-ruin-game-everyone__trashed','','','2016-10-10 14:57:08','2016-10-10 21:57:08','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?p=3698',0,'post','',0),(3699,7,'2016-10-10 14:59:05','2016-10-10 21:59:05','<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>When making the invite list for your next board game night you\'ll definitely want to keep the following players off the list...</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<b>The Rule Nazi </b>- Yes, we know that the game has rules and they are important... but these people take it to the extreme.  It\'s as if nothing makes them happier than telling you how you\'re playing the game \"ALL WRONG\".\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i>No fun for you!</i>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i><b>Solution: </b></i>Take the rule book away and feed them enough junk food to put them into a food coma\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<b>The Perplexed</b> - You\'ll know this player by the constant look of confusion on their face.  It\'s not just the number of questions they ask that is annoying, its the fact that they ask the same questions over and over and over.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i><b>Solution: </b></i>Have them play together with another player for the first game so they can learn\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<b>The Trash Talker</b> - We all love a little smack talk. In fact, it is part of what makes gaming so great.  But this is the type of person who takes being competitive way too far.  It\'s supposed to be fun, right?!\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<i>Odoyle rules!</i>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div><i><b>Solution:</b></i> All players gang up on this player to make sure they never, ever win</div>\r\n<div><b>The Slow Poke</b> - There is always that one player that thinks every move through for waaaaaaaayyyy too long.  Then when they finally do take their turn you wonder what the heck they were thinking about that entire time.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div><i><b>Solution:</b></i> Agree upon a set time limit for each turn and use a timer</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div><b>The Table Flipper</b> - The most hanus of all board game ruiners are the table flippers.  We all hate to lose, but these poor sports take it to a whole new level.</div>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<div><b><i>Solution:</i></b> Super glue the table to the floor, or better yet, don\'t invite them at all!</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\nDISCLAIMER: As I write this I realize I\'m probably all of these on certain days.  Except a table flipper.  That\'s just not cool.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>IMAGE CREDIT: giphy.com</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>','5 Board Game Player Types that Ruin the Game for Everyone','','trash','open','open','','5-board-game-player-types-ruin-game-everyone__trashed-2','','','2016-10-10 15:12:34','2016-10-10 22:12:34','',0,'https://boardgames.com/?p